alse, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-31T03:59:07Z", "username": "Pranshu", "text": "Disclaimer: now that I think about it, this is probably the most obscure hint for the funda 🫣\nQ10: Published in 1916, this foundational modernist novel follows the intellectual and spiritual awakening of a protagonist whose name invokes the master craftsman of Greek mythology. The narrative famously mirrors the subject's growth, beginning with the fragmented, sensory language of a small child and evolving into the complex aesthetic theories of a university student. The story tracks a young man’s struggle to break free from the \"nets\" of nationality, language, and religion in turn-of-the-century Ireland. Key moments include a terrifyingly vivid Jesuit sermon on the pains of Hell and a secular epiphany on a beach that leads him to reject the priesthood. This work serves as the essential prelude to the author's later, more experimental odyssey through the streets of Dublin on a single June day. Name the author and the novel?", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-31T03:59:33Z", "username": "Nikhil Borra", "text": "Joyce", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-31T03:59:39Z", "username": "Nikhil Borra", "text": "Ulysses", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-31T03:59:40Z", "username": "Khandoba", "text": "Master craftsman is Hephaestus?", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}]